{{!
    @template tool_openapi/documentation/viewer

    The interactive viewer. The container starts empty: the bundled Swagger
    UI fills it once it has fetched the document, which is why the page also
    loads tool_openapi/viewer.

    The library is included with a plain script tag rather than through
    $PAGE->requires->js(), which would route it through lib/javascript.php
    and run an already-minified 1.5MB bundle through core_minify a second
    time -- that produces truncated, unparseable output. Placed before the
    container, and so ahead of the AMD call the footer emits, which is what
    the module needs to find the global it defines.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading - Section heading
    * headingdesc - Sentence under the heading
    * tokenhint - Pre-rendered notification: what a reader needs before Try it out will work
    * restwarning - Pre-rendered notification, empty unless the REST protocol is off
    * backurl / backlabel - The way back to the documentation page
    * libraryurl - The bundled Swagger UI script
    * elementid - Id of the container Swagger UI renders into
    * protocols - REST / RESTful switch (label, url, active), empty without webservice_restful

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Interactive viewer",
        "headingdesc": "Browse every function this site exposes.",
        "tokenhint": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">Paste a token into the wstoken field.</div>",
        "restwarning": "",
        "backurl": "https://example.com/documentation/index.php",
        "backlabel": "Back to documentation",
        "libraryurl": "https://example.com/thirdparty/swagger-ui/swagger-ui-bundle.js",
        "elementid": "tool_openapi-viewer",
        "protocols": [
            {"label": "REST", "url": "https://example.com/viewer.php?protocol=rest", "active": true},
            {"label": "RESTful", "url": "https://example.com/viewer.php?protocol=restful", "active": false}
        ]
    }
}}
{{> tool_openapi/local/back_link}}

<h3>{{heading}}</h3>
<p class="text-muted">{{headingdesc}}</p>

{{#protocols.0}}
<div class="btn-group mb-3" role="group">
    {{#protocols}}
    <a href="{{url}}" class="btn btn-sm {{#active}}btn-primary{{/active}}{{^active}}btn-outline-primary{{/active}}"{{#active}} aria-current="page"{{/active}}>{{label}}</a>
    {{/protocols}}
</div>
{{/protocols.0}}

{{{restwarning}}}
{{{tokenhint}}}

<script src="{{libraryurl}}"></script>
<div id="{{elementid}}"></div>
